WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.420
Good morning, California.

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.560
It is such a great day to be
a community college champion.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.780
I want to share three
ideas with you today.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:13.400
Three ideas that can fundamentally
change higher education as we know it.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:18.280
Three ideas that can serve
every working Californian.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.580
Idea one, recognize what people know.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.980
Imagine a veteran who has spent eight
years operating sophisticated technology,

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.360
leading teams and
solving complex problems.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:36.220
and then walks into a community
college and is told, welcome, start

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.240
from the beginning.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.720
Really? Or an electrician
with 15 years of experience.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.615
Why should they have to prove their

00:00:45.615 --> 00:00:47.820
knowledge by sitting
through courses covering

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.060
what they already know?

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.700
We at the California Community Colleges
must recognize what people know.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:01:00.180
Today, more than 55 ,000 students,
including nearly 30 ,000 veterans,

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.679
have been documented in our CPL

00:01:02.679 --> 00:01:05.840
infrastructure with
faculty-approved credit

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:06.840
opportunities.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:11.060
So we are already
recognizing what people know.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:18.040
And as AI transforms jobs and careers,
people will continually acquire new

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.560
skills in new settings.

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:25.360
Our colleges must be ready to recognize
that learning wherever it happens.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:30.620
Idea number two, give
students back their time.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.740
Time is perhaps the most precious
resource our students have.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.500
For a working parent, one less course
means more evenings with your children.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:45.620
For a veteran, one less semester means
an earlier start to a new career.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:52.260
Our CPL Initiative projects
approximately $390 million in immediate

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:58.020
student savings and over $1 .5
billion in economic impact over

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:03.900
20 years. Those are impressive
numbers, but behind every dollar saved

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:08.400
is something we cannot put a
price on, a student's time.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:14.800
So let's give students back their time,
and when we shorten the distance between

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:20.280
what someone already knows and the
credential they need, we accelerate

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.920
economic mobility for individuals,
for families, and for communities.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:32.320
Idea number three, make CPL a standard
part of the student experience

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:35.720
across all 116 colleges.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:40.700
You see, now comes our next big challenge.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.560
How do we take CPL to scale?

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:48.740
Imagine a student applying to college
and being welcomed with these words,

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:50.100
Congratulations!

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:56.860
Your prior learning has already earned
you 15 college credits toward a program of

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:02.800
study. Complete just one more course,
and you qualify for a Certificate

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:07.620
of Achievement, and you are already
on your way to an Associate's degree.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:14.560
Imagine technology identifying
those opportunities and our faculty

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:19.600
validating the learning and our
counselors guiding students forward.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.746
Now imagine making this
the standard student

00:03:23.746 --> 00:03:26.480
experience across all of our colleges.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:32.220
California has invested
another $42 million

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:38.040
in the 2026-27 budget to help build

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.700
this future, this dream.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:46.580
We have the resources, we have the faculty
expertise, and we have the momentum.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:52.460
Now we need the systems and the commitment
to bring this opportunity to every

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.340
student. So let's just do it.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:04:01.060
Make CPL a standard part of the
student experience across all

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:02.760
116 colleges.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:09.160
Our goal is to reach 250
,000 Californians through CPL

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:10.700
by 2030.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:16.980
So as you gather for this seventh
Summit, I hope these three

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.000
ideas stay with you.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:25.520
Recognize what people know, give
students back their time, and make CPL a

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.080
standard part of the student experience.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:31.597
To our faculty, counselors, classified

00:04:31.597 --> 00:04:34.720
professionals, college
leaders, and partners

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:39.300
who have brought us this
far, a big thank you.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:45.720
We have a remarkable opportunity to
change how California values learning and

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.360
values experience.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:53.520
After all, the California Community
Colleges, we take care of our students,

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:58.320
we take care of our communities,
and we take care of our planet.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.780
Our time is now.

